ixed-minimizer construction uses that same gamma before any finite choices are frozen. Its annotated support edge exposes the conditional argument while discharging the supplied manuscript admissibility and minimizer premises only within this use. The binding is authored source correspondence, not mechanically checked witness equality or proof acceptance.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-classical-primary","scalar-r2-26-cite-minimizer-attainment"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.classical_primary","kind":"goal","label":"Closed existence of a near-optimal bounded synthesis input","locator":"03-classical-optimization.tex:3–75, 220–254, 553–608; prop:classical-near-optimum; 06-assembly.tex:7–17 and rem:order-of-choices","source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-qaoa-scalar","statement":"For every ε>0 and η_H>0 there exists a zero-temperature minimizer γ and one common finite set of cutoff, scalar-mesh, smoothing, trigonometric and color/helper choices producing a centered m_col with |m_col|≤1, E(m_col)≥P_*−ε and 0<p_H<η_H. Its bounded odd angle/column formulas have the prescribed exclusions and bounded continuous derivatives conditional on labels. Every coefficient, depth, law and function is fixed independently of D,n,J.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.classical_primary","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.classical_primary","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_primary%22%2C%22circuit.bounded_trigonometric%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_primary%22%2C%22circuit.bounded_trigonometric%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.bounded_trigonometric"},{"application":{"premise_bindings":[{"assumption_id":"scalar.paper_minimizer","binding_names":["gamma"],"rationale":"Attainment supplies one gamma minimizing the same manuscript Parisi functional; all later cutoff, mesh, smoothing, trigonometric and color choices are made for this gamma.","supplier_id":"scalar.minimizer_attainment"},{"assumption_id":"scalar.paper_admissible","binding_names":["gamma"],"rationale":"The attaining gamma is a member of the same class U, so its admissibility is supplied with its minimality. Pure zero-field SK and the specified normalization remain the fixed domain of both statements. No SKSupport-to-SKValue model transport is asserted.","supplier_id":"scalar.minimizer_attainment"}],"rationale":"The manuscript fixes an attained minimizer before constructing the bounded formula (the concluding construction is at lines 553–608). Applying the conditional construction to this common gamma supplies the closed existential input. The application is authored and remains subject to semantic review.","remaining_assumption_ids":[],"shared_bindings":{"gamma":"one minimizer gamma in the manuscript's zero-field pure-SK admissible class U, chosen by attainment and used throughout the fixed-minimizer construction"},"source_span":{"end_line":41,"source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-qaoa-scalar","start_line":23},"status":"authored"},"application_metadata_scope":"remaining_assumption_ids is authored historical metadata, not an effective obligation audit; path-local suppression may be lifted for retained formal dependencies.","derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.classical_primary","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.classical_primary%22%2C%22circuit.classical_fixed_minimizer%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256